    "description": "Rimfire Redirectinator 9000: Laffs Dynamics\n\nBEHOLD\n\nDR.LAFFSALOTS REDIRECTINATOR... 9000!!!!!\n\nA 1/2x28 threaded tiny flashcan for rimfire short barreled firearms. \n\nTested with a Beretta 21A Bobcat Covert; having such a short barrel (2.4in) it was the perfect testbed for attempting to reduce flash. \n\nComes with a 3D printable hand wrench for easy installation and removal of the muzzle device. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 8+\nInfill: 80%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 18%\n\n\n\nCredits: \n\nPunished_DP_Roberts: Test fired a Beretta 21A Covert with the flashcan design, provided video footage and visual feedback of design's performance. \n\n\n\nNote: This was meant to be uploaded almost a year ago. Idk how I somehow publicly released the XL variant, yet forgot the release this as the original",
